    closed, on the transport its Create Request came on, so data the server sent for it before
    it saw the decline is dropped instead of ending the session ("access to non existing DVC
    channel"). GNOME Remote Desktop sends on AUDIO_PLAYBACK_DVC right after asking to open it,
    and a session ended about a second after connecting. A channel remembered again on the same
    transport moves to the newest end of the history instead of taking another place, and a
    Soft-Sync request remembers the closed channels it lists only after it checked them all.
    Upstream IronRDP's own fix, a7ab89bd84 (#2341), line for line.
  - The package's Cargo.toml.orig, Cargo.lock and .cargo_vcs_info.json are left out: they are
    not used by a build from a path.
