ironrdp-session

ZestSSH's copy of ironrdp-session (this folder) is a fork of the crate as published.

  ironrdp-session 0.13.0, https://github.com/Devolutions/IronRDP (crates/ironrdp-session)
  Copyright (c) Devolutions Inc. and the IronRDP contributors; Teleport
  Licensed under the MIT license or the Apache License 2.0, at your option: LICENSE-MIT and
  LICENSE-APACHE beside this file are the crate's own.

Forked on 13 November 2026 by Affluent Labs LLC for ZestSSH (4.0, RDP), and used in place of the
crates.io package through [patch.crates-io] in zest_native's Cargo.toml. What came from the crate
stays under its licence; our changes follow this folder's licence too (MIT or Apache-2.0), so
they can go upstream as they are.

Why a fork: this crate reads what a server sends once a session is up (screen updates, pointers,
the channels), and ZestSSH's fuzzing of it (fuzz/fuzz_targets/rdp_session.rs) finds inputs that
make it panic. The app's library ends the whole app on a panic, so each is fixed here, at its
source, the day it is found, and listed below to be sent upstream. The same for what a server can
make it keep in memory without limit, where the place to say no is inside this crate.

What changed against 0.13.0, and nothing else (each line marked "ZestSSH" in the source, but
for the one change taken from upstream as it is):

  - src/rfx.rs (19 November 2026): RemoteFX tile and clip rectangles no longer wrap u16 on what
    a server sends (a large tile index, a zero width or height): tile positions are checked in
    u16 and clip rectangles computed in u32 with exclusive bounds held to the channel; a tile
    starting past the u16 range is skipped, one crossing its end is cut there. A release build
    wrapped (a tile drawn in the wrong place), a debug build panicked. Upstream IronRDP's own
    fix, 56d691e3ff (#2096), line for line.
  - src/fast_path.rs, process_surface_commands: a Set Surface Bits or Stream Surface Bits command
    whose destination rectangle is empty or inverted (right <= left or bottom <= top) is an
    error. Its right and bottom edges had 1 taken off unchecked: with right 0 that wrapped to
    65535 (and panicked where overflow is checked). Found 13 November 2026 by the first seed of
    rdp_session, 31 bytes after the sign-in.
  - src/fast_path.rs, CompleteData::append_data: a fast-path update sent in fragments may come
    to MAX_FRAGMENTED_UPDATE (8 MiB, the MaxRequestSize the client's capabilities say) and no
    more; a longer one is an error. Fragments that never ended with a last one were kept without
    any limit, for as long as a server sent them. Found by reading, 13 November 2026.
  - src/fast_path.rs, process_pointer_update: a pointer shape larger than MAX_POINTER_SIDE (384
    pixels a side, the protocol's largest) or for a cache index of POINTER_CACHE_SIZE (32, what
    the client's capabilities say) or more is not decoded and not kept; the default pointer is
    reported instead (refuse_pointer). The decoder took any size and the cache any of 65,536
    indexes, so a server could have the client keep thousands of large shapes, each 16 times
    the bytes sent for it at 1 bit a pixel. Only reached where the application turns the
    server's pointer on (enable_server_pointer). Found by reading, 13 November 2026.
  - The package's Cargo.toml.orig, Cargo.lock and .cargo_vcs_info.json are left out: they are
    not used by a build from a path.
  - One long dash in a comment (src/active_stage.rs) is a plain hyphen: this repository keeps
    none. No code changed by that.

Nothing here has been sent upstream yet. A new IronRDP release means this folder is made again
from that release with the changes it still needs.
